{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-80f91d18-c96c-4469-9d87-211eddb6e467","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-916313b5438f1e20","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8007-yva43hx5/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8007-E004.md","content":"# Feature Store management views: list, detail/inspect, delete, and status tracking\n\n## Description\n\nBuild the Feature Store admin management pages in the odh-dashboard frontend: a list page showing all `FeatureStore` instances across namespaces the user can access, a read-only detail/inspect view of any instance's full configuration and status, an admin-initiated delete flow with confirmation dialog, and real-time deployment-status tracking. Read data comes from the existing `/api/featurestores` proxy and Kubernetes watch/list patterns; deletes go through the existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Management list page: one row per `FeatureStore` CR in the admin's accessible namespaces, showing name, namespace, deployment status, and creation timestamp. Row actions: inspect and delete (delete shown to admins only).\n- Status tracking: deployment status derived from `.status.conditions`, displayed as \"Deploying\" (or equivalent) until all conditions are met, then \"Ready\", updating within the dashboard's existing watch/poll cycle without manual refresh — so an admin can track progress immediately after creating an instance.\n- Read-only detail/inspect view: full `FeatureStore` CR spec and status — configured backends (online/offline store type, registry type), authorization mode, scaling settings, TLS status, materialization schedule, and deployment conditions — rendered without truncation, with a link to the Feast UI Route (if available) for browsing feature metadata.\n- Delete flow: confirmation dialog, then a `DELETE` request via the `/api/k8s/*` pass-through for the `FeatureStore` CR; the feast-operator handles cleanup of owned resources (Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, CronJobs, HPAs, PDBs, RBAC, Routes) via finalizers.\n- Viewer (non-admin) gating: non-admin users see the list and detail views but the Create button and Delete action are not displayed; write controls hidden based on the dashboard's existing admin status check and `secureAdminRoute` middleware.\n- Feature flag gating: the pages render only when the Feature Store admin UI flag is enabled in `OdhDashboardConfig`.\n- Air-gapped support: no form options, assets, or data fetches require external network access; all rendering uses bundled static assets.\n- Implementation follows the finalized UXD wireframes and interaction patterns for the list page, detail view, and delete dialog.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given FeatureStore instances exist in namespaces the admin can access, the list page shows all of them with name, namespace, status, and creation timestamp, measured by the list matching `kubectl get featurestores -A` for the admin's accessible namespaces.\n- Given an instance was just created, the status column reflects `.status.conditions` within the dashboard's watch/poll cycle, transitioning from deploying to ready without manual refresh.\n- Given the admin clicks an instance, the detail view renders all spec fields (backends, auth mode, scaling, TLS, materialization schedule) and current status conditions in read-only form, without truncation.\n- Given the admin confirms deletion in the dialog, the `FeatureStore` CR is deleted via the Kubernetes API and operator-owned resources are cleaned up, measured by the instance disappearing from the list and `kubectl get featurestore <name> -n <ns>` returning NotFound.\n- Given a non-admin (viewer) user, the list and detail views render without the Create button or Delete action.\n- The pages function on a disconnected/air-gapped cluster with no external connectivity (no external asset or option fetches).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- P0: view all FeatureStore instances across accessible namespaces (list page).\n- P0: inspect the configuration of any FeatureStore instance (detail view).\n- P0: delete a FeatureStore instance with confirmation dialog (delete flow).\n- P0: deployment progress / readiness status visible and updating in real time (status tracking).\n- P1: non-admin viewers can browse instances but cannot create or delete (viewer gating — bundled with the P0 list/detail work: same UI surfaces).\n- P1: disconnected/air-gapped operation (bundled: property of the same frontend implementation).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":48941,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9bbdd7d948b51495","agent_id":"adbe888c35f5fced7","session_id":"6ff6a9df-bf42-414a-b8db-47534bab81b1","uuid":"daaf3e12-74cb-495f-9404-2f938201abaa","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:03:25.211Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8007"}
