{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ce7fe2448bbe534","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E001\n3\ttitle: Validate FeatureStore CRD form-field scope, backend restrictions, and prototype\n4\t  alignment for TP\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n6\tcomponent: Feature Store\n7\tteam: Feature Store Engineering\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tdependencies: []\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 1\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Validate FeatureStore CRD form-field scope, backend restrictions, and prototype alignment for TP\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tThis investigation resolves the open questions that gate the Feature Store admin create-wizard work: which `FeatureStore` CRD (feast.dev/v1) fields the TP create form should expose, which store-backend combinations should be restricted in the form, whether the existing engineering prototype (odh-dashboard draft PR #7013) aligns with the strategy's formal implementation path, and whether the CRD schema is stable for the RHOAI 3.5 cycle. It consolidates the Feature Store Engineering consultation already called for by the strategy (validate CRD schema coverage for the form wizard, verify prototype alignment) into a single deliverable: a validated form-field and validation specification for the TP wizard, plus a prototype-reuse assessment.\n31\t\n32\t## Scope\n33\t\n34\t- Enumerate the `FeatureStore` CRD (feast.dev/v1) spec surface relevant to the admin form: registry type, online store backend (Redis, PostgreSQL, DynamoDB, SQLite), offline store backend, authorization mode (OIDC vs Kubernetes RBAC), TLS settings, scaling configuration (replicas, HPA), and materialization CronJob scheduling — sourced from the CRD OpenAPI schema (architecture context: `feast.md`, CRDs section).\n35\t- Recommend the TP form-field set: full CRD spec vs curated subset, with rationale for each included/excluded field, for PM ratification.\n36\t- Document backend combinations that should be restricted or flagged in the form (e.g., SQLite as development-only, not production-suitable) and the validation rules that follow from CRD schema constraints.\n37\t- Assess the prototype (odh-dashboard draft PR #7013): document where it aligns with the strategy's approach (K8s API pass-through CRUD, PatternFly wizard, admin/viewer gating) and where it diverges, and state what can be reused vs rebuilt.\n38\t- Confirm with Feature Store Engineering that the feast.dev/v1 CRD schema will not undergo breaking changes during the RHOAI 3.5 cycle (v1alpha1 is deprecated; v1 is the target), or flag any expected changes and their impact on the form mapping.\n39\t- Confirm the feast-operator reconciles dashboard-created `FeatureStore` CRs identically to kubectl-created ones and that CRD webhook validation is sufficient for UI-submitted resources (the operator watches the CRD, not the creation method; reconfirm and record).\n40\t\n41\t## Acceptance Criteria\n42\t\n43\t- A form-field specification is delivered that enumerates the TP create-form field set (or confirms the full set), covering at minimum namespace, registry type, online store backend, offline store backend, authorization mode, and scaling parameters, with each field traced to its CRD schema definition.\n44\t- A documented list of restricted or discouraged backend combinations with rationale, suitable for deriving form validation rules.\n45\t- A prototype alignment assessment that states, for each major capability, whether the draft PR implementation can be reused, adapted, or must be rebuilt.\n46\t- CRD v1 stability for the 3.5 cycle is confirmed in writing, or expected changes are documented with their impact on the form-field mapping.\n47\t- Every question above has a defined answer source (CRD OpenAPI schema, prototype source code, Feature Store Engineering confirmation) recorded with the answer.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- Enables the P0 HLR \"deploy a new FeatureStore instance via guided form wizard\" by resolving what the wizard must cover (field set, validation rules, implementation reference). Does not implement the HLR itself.\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8bb5f9cf8a8fdc6","agent_id":"aa4b698e26a62b72b","session_id":"6ff6a9df-bf42-414a-b8db-47534bab81b1","uuid":"bb0b8e0a-cb40-4d1e-a415-b47248e7bdbd","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:06:29.991Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ce7fe2448bbe534","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8007 decomposition"}
