{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a57b7f66295e7243","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E003\n3\ttitle: Dashboard RBAC extension and feature-flag manifests for Feature Store admin\n4\t  operations\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n6\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n7\tteam: Dashboard/Frontend Engineering\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tdependencies: []\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 5\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Dashboard RBAC extension and feature-flag manifests for Feature Store admin operations\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tExtend the odh-dashboard's RBAC and configuration manifests so platform administrators can create, update, patch, and delete `FeatureStore` custom resources (feast.dev/v1) through the dashboard, and gate the new admin UI behind an `OdhDashboardConfig` feature flag for progressive rollout. This covers the backend/manifests portion of the strategy's odh-dashboard changes — no new backend routes are needed, since CRUD uses the existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through proxy that forwards the authenticated user's token to the Kubernetes API.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Update `manifests/core-bases/base/sa-rbac/cluster-role.yaml` to add `create, update, patch, delete` verbs for `feast.dev/featurestores` to the dashboard's ClusterRole (the existing role already grants `get, list, watch`). The `featurestore-editor-role` ClusterRole defined by the feast-operator (architecture context: `feast.md`, RBAC section) serves as the reference for the minimum required permission set.\n39\t- Validate the RBAC mechanism assumption flagged \"needs validation\" in the strategy: confirm whether extending the dashboard ClusterRole is the correct mechanism for granting platform admins write access, given that CRUD requests through `/api/k8s/*` are authorized against the user's own forwarded token (architecture context: `odh-dashboard.md`, Authentication & Authorization), or whether admin role bindings (e.g., binding the feast-operator's editor role) are required instead. Implement the validated mechanism.\n40\t- Add the feature flag default in `OdhDashboardConfig` (e.g., a `featureStore` flag) gating the admin UI; default off so clusters without the Feast component enabled see no UI changes.\n41\t- Ensure the viewer tier continues to work read-only through the existing `featurestore-viewer-role` ClusterRole from the feast-operator (get, list, watch on featurestores and featurestores/status) — no changes to viewer permissions.\n42\t- Manifest-only changes: no new Go BFF module, preserving FIPS compliance (Node.js 22 / UBI 9 base) per the strategy's NFRs.\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- A platform administrator can create and delete `FeatureStore` CRs from the dashboard via the `/api/k8s/*` pass-through using their own token, measured by successful CRUD operations performed as an admin through the dashboard proxy.\n47\t- A non-admin (viewer) token attempting to create or delete a `FeatureStore` CR is rejected by the Kubernetes API (viewer retains only get/list/watch via the existing viewer role).\n48\t- The RBAC mechanism validation is documented (admin role bindings vs ClusterRole extension), and the implemented mechanism matches it.\n49\t- The admin UI is gated behind an `OdhDashboardConfig` feature flag, off by default; clusters without the Feast component enabled show no UI changes.\n50\t- No new backend routes, no new BFF sidecar container, and no new external network connections are introduced.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- Enables the P0 HLRs \"deploy a new FeatureStore instance from the dashboard\" and \"delete a FeatureStore instance from the dashboard\" (write-path RBAC).\n55\t- Supports the P1 viewer HLR: non-admin users keep read-only access enforced at the Kubernetes API level, not just in the UI.\n56\t- Implements the security NFRs (K8s RBAC via forwarded bearer token, kube-rbac-proxy, `secureAdminRoute` middleware complement).\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8bb5f9cf8a8fdc6","agent_id":"aa4b698e26a62b72b","session_id":"6ff6a9df-bf42-414a-b8db-47534bab81b1","uuid":"1c2ebb0f-e135-447d-a903-058031272b1a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:06:31.387Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a57b7f66295e7243","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8007 decomposition"}
