e button\") and E005 (\"non-admin users do not see the Create action\") — incidental overlap on one control, not duplicate construction of a surface.\n\n### 4. Type Correctness (0/2)\n\n**Major issue — missing gate metadata on E002.** E002 (UXD wireframes) lists the Investigation epic E001 in its `dependencies`, but its frontmatter has `gated_by: null` and `gate_failure_impact: null`. The decomposition's own DAG justification labels the E001→E002 edge a \"True gate (`rewrite`)\" — the investigation's field-set outcome changes what the wizard wireframes must cover — so by the criteria this is an Investigation dependency without `gated_by`, a major issue: automated pipeline consumers detect gates via `gated_by` and will silently miss this one. The inconsistency is internal to the decomposition: E005, gated by the same investigation for the same reason, correctly carries `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-8007-E001` plus a populated `gate_failure_impact` (action: rewrite, with fallback approach). Fix: set `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-8007-E001` and a `gate_failure_impact` (action: rewrite; fallback: re-scope the wizard wireframes to the validated field set) on E002. All other typing is correct: E001 is a genuine Investigation (its field-set/backend-restriction/prototype-alignment outcomes change downstream scope, with two dependents); E002–E006 produce concrete artifacts; E005's `gated_by` is in its direct dependencies; E006's Rule 11 dependencies are scheduling edges correctly lacking gates.\n\n### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (1/2)\n\nAll six ai-signals files are present, each epic uses the rubric matching its type (E001 carries `investigation_signals`; E002–E006 carry `ai_signals`), and frontmatter values match the rationale tables. Two arguable signal values: (1) E002 scores `open_questions: 0` with the rationale that the gating unknown is \"resolved by the upstream investigation dependency,\" while E005 scores `open_questions: -1` for the same still-unresolved E001 outcome (\"gated..