low in the RHOAI admin guide | Implementation (docs-authoring) | Documentation Team | P1 |\n31\t\n32\t## Component Mapping Notes\n33\t\n34\t- `odh-dashboard` (frontend, backend, kustomize manifests) maps to canonical Jira component **AI Core Dashboard** — the closest canonical name in `.context/rhai-components.txt`; the three strategy rows are all the same repo/component owned by the same team, so they are decomposed by sub-system boundary rather than by row.\n35\t- `feast-operator` maps to canonical component **Feature Store**. It is a **passive component** in this strategy (no code changes expected). Because a different team (Feature Store Engineering) performs the validation, the validation work becomes its own epic (E001) rather than an acceptance criterion on a dashboard epic.\n36\t- UXD design assets → canonical component **UXD**; admin guide content → canonical component **Documentation**.\n37\t- Both `odh-dashboard` and `feast` have architecture context files (`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/odh-dashboard.md`, `feast.md`) — no new-component onboarding chain is needed; no repo-onboarding, license-validation, or konflux-onboarding epics apply (Prerequisites table marks them Not applicable — changes are within the existing odh-dashboard build pipeline).\n38\t\n39\t## Dependency DAG\n40\t\n41\t```mermaid\n42\tgraph TD\n43\t  E001[RHAISTRAT-8007-E001 Investigation: CRD form scope] --> E002[RHAISTRAT-8007-E002 UXD design]\n44\t  E001 --> E005[RHAISTRAT-8007-E005 Create wizard]\n45\t  E002 --> E004[RHAISTRAT-8007-E004 Management views]\n46\t  E002 --> E005\n47\t  E002 --> E006[RHAISTRAT-8007-E006 Docs]\n48\t  E003[RHAISTRAT-8007-E003 RBAC + feature flag] --> E006\n49\t  E004 --> E006\n50\t  E005 --> E006\n51\t```\n52\t\n53\t## DAG Justification\n54\t\n55\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n56\t|------|------|-----------|\n57\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 3 / Rule 13 | The investigation produces the TP form-field specification the wizard wireframes are designed against; the field-set outcome changes what the design covers. True gate (`rewrite`). |\n58\t| E001 → E005 | Rule 3 | The field-subset, backend-restriction, and prototype-alignment outcomes change what the create wizard implements. True gate (`rewrite`) — recorded as `gated_by` on E005. Both bounded outcomes (full field set vs curated subset) land in the same wizard epic with different scope, so no conditional branch files are warranted. |\n59\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 12/13 | The list/detail/delete views build against the finalized UXD designs (strategy dependency table: \"form wizard and list page designs required before implementation\"). |\n60\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 12/13 | The create wizard builds against the finalized UXD designs. |\n61\t| E002, E003, E004, E005 → E006 | Rule 11 | `docs-authoring` is blocked by all Implementation epics; docs describe what was built. Per the docs-authoring priority exception, E006 is P1 (strategy frontmatter priority `Major` → P1) and does not push priority upstream. |\n62\t| E003 ∥ E004, E003 ∥ E005 (no edge) | Rule 15 / Rule 13 | RBAC manifest changes and frontend pages are different areas of the same repo with no build-against artifact — the frontend does not compile against the ClusterRole. RBAC availability is enforced as an acceptance-criteria gate on E004/E005 (CRUD succeeds as admin, rejected as viewer), never as a DAG edge. |\n63\t| E001 ∥ E003, E001 ∥ E004 (no edge) | — | The investigation only gates work whose scope depends on its answers (wizard design, wizard). The views epic renders whatever CR fields exist and the RBAC epic's scope is fixed by the strategy's technical approach. |\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n66\t\n67\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n68\t|-----|----------|---------|\n69\t| Deploy a new FeatureStore instance via guided form wizard (namespace, registry type, online/offline store backend, authorization mode, scaling) | P0 | E005 (enabled by E001, E002, E003) |\n70\t| View all FeatureStore instances across accessible namespaces with name, namespace, status, creation time | P0 | E004 |\n71\t| Inspect configuration of any FeatureStore instance in read-only detail view | P0 | E004 |\n72\t| Delete a FeatureStore instance with confirmation dialog | P0 | E004 (write path enabled by E003) |\n73\t| Deployment progress (readiness from `.status.conditions`) visible and updating in real time | P0 | E004 |\n74\t| Non-admin (viewer) users can browse but cannot create/delete | P1 | E004 (bundled: same list/detail UI surfaces as P0 work — not independently deferrable) |\n75\t| Admin UI functions in disconnected/air-gapped environments | P1 | E004, E005 (bundled: a property of the same implementation — static assets, no external fetches) |\n76\t| Form validation provides inline guidance for CRD schema constraints | P2 | E005 (bundled: same form surface as the P0 wizard; UX polish of the same implementation) |\n77\t\n78\tAll HLRs covered; no orphaned requirements. No priority splits: the P1 viewer-gating and air-gapped HLRs share UI surfaces and implementation with their P0 counterparts, and the P2 validation HLR is UX polish of the P0 wizard — each fails the \"distinct and deferrable\" test (independent user value AND no shared UI surface).\n79\t\n80\t## Open-Question Disposition\n81\t\n82\t| Open question | Disposition |\n83\t|---------------|-------------|\n84\t| Create form: all CRD fields vs curated subset for TP | Investigation E001 (changes what the wizard and its design cover). Final curation ratified by PM. |\n85\t| Backend combinations to restrict in the form (e.g., SQLite dev-only) | Investigation E001 (same consultation and deliverable as the field-scope question — form validation spec). |\n86\t| Prototype PR #7013 alignment vs divergence | Investigation E001 (same deliverable — prototype assessment informing reuse). |\n87\t| FeatureStore CRD v1 stability in the 3.5 cycle (assumption \"needs validation\") | Investigation E001 (same consultation). |\n88\t| UXD timeline for wireframes | Not an Investigation — a scheduling unknown, not a technical unknown; it does not change which epics exist. Flagged as a health warning (design gates all P0 frontend work). |\n89\t| Edit capability for deployed instances (mutable fields) | Already resolved by the strategy: Out-of-Scope explicitly limits TP to create + inspect + delete. No epic created. |\n90\t| Performance targets for TP | Not an Investigation — a PM decision that does not change epic structure; if targets are set they become acceptance criteria on the views/wizard epics. Flagged as a health warning. |\n91\t| Admin RBAC write-path assumption (\"needs validation\": admin role bindings vs ClusterRole extension) | Implementation detail — folded into E003 scope as a validation step and acceptance criterion (Step 6.5: validation of assumptions is resolved by the team when starting the work; the epic exists and delivers the same outcome either way). |\n92\t\n93\t## Health Warnings\n94\t\n95\t- **Schedule risk on the design gate**: the `needs-uxd` label is present but no UXD design sprint is scheduled, and the UXD design epic gates all P0 frontend implementation. The strategy's own mitigation (use prototype PR #7013 as a starting design reference) is captured in E002 scope. Non-blocking; human verification of the UXD timeline recommended.\n96\t- **Embedded PM decision**: the final TP field curation produced by E001 requires PM ratification (open question owner: PM + Feature Store Engineering). The investigation delivers the technical envelope and a recommendation; the decision step is human.\n97\t- **RBAC mechanism tension (non-blocking)**: the strategy prescribes extending the odh-dashboard ClusterRole while also stating that CRUD is enforced via the user's forwarded token through the `/api/k8s/*` impersonation proxy (architecture context `odh-dashboard.md` confirms user-token impersonation). Which mechanism actually grants platform admins write verbs on `feast.dev/featurestores` is marked \"needs validation\" in the assumptions; E003 includes validating and implementing the correct mechanism as explicit scope.\n98\t- **Performance targets undefined**: no performance targets exist for the admin UI; deferred to PM. If set (e.g., list-page load with 100+ instances), they become ACs on the views epic — no epic structure change.\n99\t- **Scope traps**: none detected. Out-of-scope items (no new BFF sidecar, no Feast UI embedding, no edit flow, no permissions UI) are consistent with the NFRs (FIPS maintained, no new Go BFF module; availability posture unchanged).\n100\t\n101\t## Tiered Delivery\n102\t\n103\tNot applicable. No external dependency has uncertain timing: the FeatureStore CRD, feast-operator reconciliation, dashboard pass-through routes, viewer/editor ClusterRoles, and PatternFly 6 all exist (dependencies table marks them \"Exists\"). The UXD design dependency is internal with a known-needed deliverable, modeled as a blocking epic rather than a tier split.\n104\t\n105\t## Notes\n106\t\n107\t- The engineering prototype (odh-dashboard draft PR #7013) is treated as reference material informing E001's assessment and E002/E005 implementation guidance — not as a hard dependency (per the strategy's dependencies table).\n108\t- QE involvement (CRUD functional testing, admin vs viewer RBAC enforcement, air-gapped validation, status accuracy) is captured as acceptance criteria on E003/E004/E005 rather than a separate epic — testing here verifies the implementing team's own deliverables rather than producing a separate artifact for a different owning team.\n109\t- Rule 23 (rollback/feature-flag AC): the admin UI is a new capability, not a replacement, but feature-flag gating is carried in E003/E004/E005 scope per the strategy's backwards-compatibility NFR (progressive rollout, no UI change on clusters without Feast).\n110\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-96c9028417b4aba7","agent_id":"aa3326b8e093fa5f7","session_id":"6ff6a9df-bf42-4