{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b201e6cab117c18","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E002\n3\ttitle: UXD wireframes and interaction design for Feature Store admin UI\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: UXD\n6\tteam: UXD Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E001\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: -1\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 4\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# UXD wireframes and interaction design for Feature Store admin UI\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tDeliver the UX design package for the Feature Store admin management surface in the RHOAI dashboard: wireframes and interaction patterns for the create-form wizard, the management list page, the read-only detail/inspect view, and the delete confirmation dialog. This addresses the `needs-uxd` requirement on the source RFE — the strategy's dependency table marks UXD design as required before frontend implementation.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Wireframes for the Feature Store management list page: instance rows (name, namespace, deployment status, creation timestamp), row actions (inspect, delete), and status indication reflecting readiness conditions.\n39\t- Interaction design for the guided create wizard: step structure covering namespace selection, registry type, online store backend, offline store backend, authorization mode, and scaling configuration, mapped to the TP field set defined by the Feature Store CRD form-field specification.\n40\t- Wireframes for the read-only detail/inspect view: configured backends, authorization mode, scaling settings, TLS status, materialization schedule, deployment conditions, and the link to the Feast UI Route for browsing feature metadata.\n41\t- Interaction pattern for the delete flow with confirmation dialog.\n42\t- Design states for admin vs non-admin (viewer) users: write controls (Create button, Delete action) hidden for viewers, consistent with the dashboard's existing admin-gating patterns.\n43\t- Design constraints: PatternFly 6 components; all assets and options must be bundled/static (disconnected/air-gapped deployments — no external resource fetches); no external network dependencies in any designed flow.\n44\t- Use the existing engineering prototype (odh-dashboard draft PR #7013) as a starting design reference to unblock work, per the strategy's risk mitigation, while formal designs are created.\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- Wireframes delivered for the list page, create wizard, detail view, and delete confirmation dialog, covering all fields in the agreed TP form-field set.\n49\t- Designs reviewed with Dashboard/Frontend Engineering and Feature Store Engineering; feedback incorporated.\n50\t- Admin and viewer design states are both specified, with write controls absent for viewers.\n51\t- No designed flow or asset depends on external network access (air-gapped compatible).\n52\t- Wizard design reflects the TP field curation agreed with PM and Feature Store Engineering.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- Enables the P0 HLRs for the guided create wizard, the management list page, the inspect view, and the delete flow by providing the designs they are built against.\n57\t- Enables the P1 viewer-browsing HLR (browse without create/delete controls) via the viewer design states.\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-96c9028417b4aba7","agent_id":"aa3326b8e093fa5f7","session_id":"6ff6a9df-bf42-414a-b8db-47534bab81b1","uuid":"34a1bc00-4c53-48c0-aa83-4ae41a6e