{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8241ee418dd1b56a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E005\n3\ttitle: Feature Store guided create wizard\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard/Frontend Engineering\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E002\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8007-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the investigation rules out the assumed CRD field scope, prototype\n16\t    reuse, or backend-combination model, the wizard's field set, validation rules,\n17\t    and how much of the prototype can be reused are re-scoped to the validated outcome;\n18\t    the epic is not removed.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 4\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Feature Store guided create wizard\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tBuild the guided create-form wizard in the odh-dashboard frontend that lets a platform administrator deploy a new Feature Store instance by filling out a form mapped to the `FeatureStore` CRD spec (feast.dev/v1) — no YAML editing or CLI access required. The wizard submits a valid `FeatureStore` CR to the Kubernetes API through the dashboard's existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through, after which deployment progress is trackable on the management list page.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- React form wizard built with PatternFly 6 components, following the finalized UXD wireframes and the TP field set defined by the FeatureStore CRD form-field specification (the validated outcome of the Feature Store Engineering consultation).\n45\t- Wizard coverage per the strategy's P0 HLR: namespace selection, registry type, online store backend, offline store backend, authorization mode, and scaling parameters — within the agreed TP field curation (full set or curated subset).\n46\t- Form field mapping derived from the `FeatureStore` CRD OpenAPI schema (feast.dev/v1); field options are static configuration choices bundled in the dashboard's static assets (no network calls to enumerate options).\n47\t- Client-side validation against CRD schema constraints with inline guidance for required fields, valid backend combinations, and scaling prerequisites; restricted/discouraged backend combinations (e.g., SQLite as development-only) are prevented or flagged per the validated restriction list.\n48\t- Server-side validation feedback: if the Kubernetes API rejects the submitted CR, the validation error is surfaced in the UI.\n49\t- Submission: create the `FeatureStore` CR via the `/api/k8s/*` pass-through using the admin's token; write access is admin-only (enforced by Kubernetes RBAC and the dashboard's `secureAdminRoute` middleware).\n50\t- Feature flag gating: the wizard is reachable only when the Feature Store admin UI flag is enabled.\n51\t- Air-gapped support: all form options, validation rules, and UI assets bundled at build time; the form fetches no external resources.\n52\t- Post-submission, the admin is returned to the management list page where deployment progress (readiness status) is visible.\n53\t- Use the engineering prototype (odh-dashboard draft PR #7013) as a reference implementation to the extent validated as aligned; rebuild what diverges.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- Given a logged-in platform admin on the Feature Store management page, clicking \"Create Feature Store\" opens the guided wizard with fields for namespace, registry type, online store backend, offline store backend, authorization mode, and scaling configuration, measured by the form rendering all agreed TP CRD fields without error and submitting a valid `FeatureStore` CR to the Kubernetes API.\n58\t- Form validation provides inline guidance for CRD schema constraints (required fields, valid backend combinations, scaling prerequisites), and invalid or restricted combinations are prevented or clearly flagged before submission.\n59\t- If the Kubernetes API rejects a submitted CR, the validation error is surfaced inline in the wizard.\n60\t- The wizard is available to platform admins only; non-admin users do not see the Create action.\n61\t- The wizard functions on a disconnected/air-gapped cluster: no form options, validation rules, or UI assets require external network access, measured by deploying a FeatureStore instance from the dashboard on an air-gapped cluster with no external connectivity.\n62\t- The wizard renders only when the Feature Store admin UI feature flag is enabled.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- P0: deploy a new FeatureStore instance from the dashboard via a guided form wizard (primary HLR for this epic).\n67\t- P1: disconnected/air-gapped operation (bundled: static asset bundling is a property of the same implementation).\n68\t- P2: form validation with inline guidance for CRD schema constraints (bundled: UX polish of the same form surface).\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-96c9028417b4aba7","agent_id":"aa3326b8e093fa5f7","session_id":"6ff6a9df-bf42-414a-b8db-47534bab81b1","uuid":"c13afae7-ac19-4e6a-9aa4-b23ab7e15856","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:10:57.126Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8241ee418dd1b56a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8007 decomposition"}
