{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9beb72804225ba2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E004\n3\ttitle: 'Feature Store management views: list, detail/inspect, delete, and status tracking'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard/Frontend Engineering\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E002\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Feature Store management views: list, detail/inspect, delete, and status tracking\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tBuild the Feature Store admin management pages in the odh-dashboard frontend: a list page showing all `FeatureStore` instances across namespaces the user can access, a read-only detail/inspect view of any instance's full configuration and status, an admin-initiated delete flow with confirmation dialog, and real-time deployment-status tracking. Read data comes from the existing `/api/featurestores` proxy and Kubernetes watch/list patterns; deletes go through the existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Management list page: one row per `FeatureStore` CR in the admin's accessible namespaces, showing name, namespace, deployment status, and creation timestamp. Row actions: inspect and delete (delete shown to admins only).\n39\t- Status tracking: deployment status derived from `.status.conditions`, displayed as \"Deploying\" (or equivalent) until all conditions are met, then \"Ready\", updating within the dashboard's existing watch/poll cycle without manual refresh — so an admin can track progress immediately after creating an instance.\n40\t- Read-only detail/inspect view: full `FeatureStore` CR spec and status — configured backends (online/offline store type, registry type), authorization mode, scaling settings, TLS status, materialization schedule, and deployment conditions — rendered without truncation, with a link to the Feast UI Route (if available) for browsing feature metadata.\n41\t- Delete flow: confirmation dialog, then a `DELETE` request via the `/api/k8s/*` pass-through for the `FeatureStore` CR; the feast-operator handles cleanup of owned resources (Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, CronJobs, HPAs, PDBs, RBAC, Routes) via finalizers.\n42\t- Viewer (non-admin) gating: non-admin users see the list and detail views but the Create button and Delete action are not displayed; write controls hidden based on the dashboard's existing admin status check and `secureAdminRoute` middleware.\n43\t- Feature flag gating: the pages render only when the Feature Store admin UI flag is enabled in `OdhDashboardConfig`.\n44\t- Air-gapped support: no form options, assets, or data fetches require external network access; all rendering uses bundled static assets.\n45\t- Implementation follows the finalized UXD wireframes and interaction patterns for the list page, detail view, and delete dialog.\n46\t- Pod-resource monitoring, per the strategy's risk mitigation for dashboard pod resource growth: monitor the dashboard pod's resource consumption (memory and startup time) in QE environments with the Feature Store admin UI enabled, confirming that adding the new frontend pages does not materially increase the dashboard container's footprint (the change adds frontend pages only — no new BFF sidecar container in the already 9+ container pod).\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Given FeatureStore instances exist in namespaces the admin can access, the list page shows all of them with name, namespace, status, and creation timestamp, measured by the list matching `kubectl get featurestores -A` for the admin's accessible namespaces.\n51\t- Given an instance was just created, the status column reflects `.status.conditions` within the dashboard's watch/poll cycle, transitioning from deploying to ready without manual refresh.\n52\t- Given the admin clicks an instance, the detail view renders all spec fields (backends, auth mode, scaling, TLS, materialization schedule) and current status conditions in read-only form, without truncation.\n53\t- Given the admin confirms deletion in the dialog, the `FeatureStore` CR is deleted via the Kubernetes API and operator-owned resources are cleaned up, measured by the instance disappearing from the list and `kubectl get featurestore <name> -n <ns>` returning NotFound.\n54\t- Given a non-admin (viewer) user, the list and detail views render without the Create button or Delete action.\n55\t- The pages function on a disconnected/air-gapped cluster with no external connectivity (no external asset or option fetches).\n56\t- Dashboard pod resource consumption (memory and startup time) is monitored in QE environments with the Feature Store admin UI enabled, and shows no material regression attributable to the new pages.\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\t- P0: view all FeatureStore instances across accessible namespaces (list page).\n61\t- P0: inspect the configuration of any FeatureStore instance (detail view).\n62\t- P0: delete a FeatureStore instance with confirmation dialog (delete flow).\n63\t- P0: deployment progress / readiness status visible and updating in real time (status tracking).\n64\t- P1: non-admin viewers can browse instances but cannot create or delete (viewer gating — bundled with the P0 list/detail work: same UI surfaces).\n65\t- P1: disconnected/air-gapped operation (bundled: property of the same frontend implementation).\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7e2f3fa4b1ae564","agent_id":"aac12a4caddf1c229","session_id":"6ff6a9df-bf42-414a-b8db-47534bab81b1","uuid":"c66274eb-5a8c-49e1-b529-bc2b93369fdc","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:13:07.368Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9beb72804225ba2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8007"}
