{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b15f70854d657be7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E006\n3\ttitle: Document the Feature Store admin UI workflow in the RHOAI admin guide\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: Documentation Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E002\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E003\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E004\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E005\n15\tai_signals:\n16\t  change_specificity: 1\n17\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n18\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n19\t  existing_foundation: 1\n20\t  open_questions: 0\n21\t  external_dependency: 0\n22\t  human_process_gates: -1\n23\t  repo_access: 1\n24\t  architecture_claims: 1\n25\tinvestigation_signals: null\n26\tai_implementability: High\n27\tai_implementability_score: 4\n28\tjira_key: null\n29\tbranch: null\n30\tgated_by: null\n31\tgate_failure_impact: null\n32\t---\n33\t# Document the Feature Store admin UI workflow in the RHOAI admin guide\n34\t\n35\t## Description\n36\t\n37\tAuthor the administrator documentation for the Feature Store admin UI: a new admin-guide topic covering how platform administrators deploy, monitor, inspect, and delete Feature Store instances from the RHOAI dashboard, including instructions for disconnected/air-gapped deployments and the admin vs viewer permission model. This is substantive new content authored through the Red Hat docs content process, not incidental touch-ups.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- New admin-guide topic: deploying a Feature Store instance via the dashboard create wizard, including the meaning of each wizard field (namespace, registry type, online/offline store backend, authorization mode, scaling) and the field-validation behavior.\n42\t- Monitoring and status tracking: reading deployment status and readiness conditions from the management list page.\n43\t- Inspecting and deleting instances from the dashboard, including the confirmation flow and operator-driven resource cleanup.\n44\t- Admin vs viewer permissions: what each role can see and do, and how access is enforced (Kubernetes RBAC via the user's token).\n45\t- Disconnected/air-gapped deployment instructions: enabling and using the admin UI on a cluster with no external connectivity.\n46\t- Feature flag enablement instructions for administrators (`OdhDashboardConfig`).\n47\t- Screenshots of the implemented UI (list page, wizard, detail view, delete dialog).\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- The admin guide documents the full workflow: create, monitor, inspect, and delete Feature Store instances from the dashboard, matching the shipped UI.\n52\t- Disconnected/air-gapped deployment instructions are included and accurate.\n53\t- The admin vs viewer permission model is documented.\n54\t- The content is technically reviewed against the implemented Feature Store admin UI by engineering before publication.\n55\t- Screenshots and steps reflect the final shipped UI, including feature-flag enablement.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- Supports all P0 HLRs (wizard deployment, list/monitor, inspect, delete) and the P1 air-gapped HLR by documenting the delivered capability. Documentation Support is listed as pending in the strategy's prerequisites; this epic fulfills it.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7e2f3fa4b1ae564","agent_id":"aac12a4caddf1c229","session_id":"6ff6a9df-bf42-414a-b8db-47534bab81b1","uuid":"e2d63507-2c00-41e5-b0c0-46afb574977f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:13:11.449Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b15f70854d657be7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8007"}
